</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The mechanics of three-dimensional cellular materials</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Royal Society of London A</source><year>1982</year><volume>382</volume><fpage>43</fpage><lpage>59</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashby</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><source>Cellular solids: structures and properties</source><year>1988</year><publisher-loc>Oxford, New York, Beijing, Frankfurt, Sao Paulo, Sydney, Tokyo, Toronto</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Pergamon Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashby</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name><name><surname>Schajer</surname><given-names>GS</given-names></name><name><surname>Robertson</surname><given-names>CI</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The mechanics of two-dimensional cellular materials</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Royal Society of London A</source><year>1982</year><volume>382</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>42</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gibson</surname><given-names>LJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Easterling</surname><given-names>KE</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahsby</surname><given-names>MF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The structure and mechanics of cork</article-title><source>Proceedings of the Royal Society of London A</source><year>1981</year><volume>377</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>117</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haberlandt</surname><given-names>GJF</given-names></name></person-group><source>Physiologische Pflanzenanatomie</source><year>1924</year><edition>6th edn</edition><publisher-loc>Leipzig</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Engelmann</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hohl</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Schopfer</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Physical extensibility of maize coleoptile cell walls: apparent plastic extensibility is due to elastic hysteresis</article-title><source>Planta</source><year>1992</year><volume>187</volume><fpage>498</fpage><lpage>504</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hotton</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><name><surname>Stein</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>An ontogenetic model for the Mississippian seed plant family Calamopityaceae</article-title><source>International Journal of Plant Sciences</source><year>1994</year><volume>155</volume><fpage>119</fpage><lpage>142</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jacobs</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The growth stresses of woody stems</article-title><source>Commonwealth Forestry Bureau Australia Bulletin</source><year>1945</year><volume>28</volume></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kraynik</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Warren</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Hilyard</surname><given-names>NC</given-names></name><name><surname>Cunningham</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The elastic behaviour of low density cellular plastics</article-title><source>Low density cellular plastics: physical basis of behaviour</source><year>1994</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Chapman and Hall</publisher-name><fpage>187</fpage><lpage>225</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>K&#x000fc;bler</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Studies on growth stresses in trees. Part I. The origin of growth stresses and the stresses in transverse direction</article-title><source>Holz als Roh-und Werkstoff</source><year>1959</year><volume>17</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>9</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>HS</given-names></name><name><surname>Hong</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lee</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name><name><surname>Kim</surname><given-names>YK</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Mechanical behavior and failure process during compressive and shear deformation of honeycomb composite at elevated temperatures</article-title><source>Journal of Materials Science</source><year>2002</year><volume>37</volume><fpage>1265</fpage><lpage>1272</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ljungdahl</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Berglund</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transverse mechanical behaviour and moisture absorption of waterlogged archaeological wood from the Vasa ship</article-title><source>Holzforschung</source><year>2007</year><volume>61</volume><fpage>279</fpage><lpage>284</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ljungdahl</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Berglund</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Burman</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Transverse anisotropy of compressive failure in European oak: a digital speckle photography study</article-title><source>Holzforschung</source><year>2006</year><volume>60</volume><fpage>190</fpage><lpage>195</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Masselter</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Rowe</surname><given-names>NP</given-names></name><name><surname>Speck</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Biomechanical reconstruction of the Carboniferous seed fern <italic>Lyginopteris oldhamia</italic>: implications for growth form reconstruction and habit</article-title><source>International Journal of Plant Sciences</source><year>2007</year><volume>168</volume><fpage>1177</fpage><lpage>1189</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Masselter</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Speck</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Salmen</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Evaluating secondary growth processes in <italic>Aristolochia macrophylla</italic> by experiments and modelling</article-title><source>Proceedings of the 5th plant biomechanics conference</source><year>2006</year><publisher-loc>Stockholm</publisher-loc><publisher-name>STFI-Packforsk AB</publisher-name><fpage>49</fpage><lpage>54</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="bib26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surna